  "demo_description": "## What this scenario simulates\n\nA 100 MW islanded data center whose demand is built only from deterministic Kubernetes, Slurm, and Ray jobs. The three scheduler cohorts hold each level for three minutes and move through approximately 2 MW background → 10 MW → 30 MW → 70 MW peak → 50 MW → 15 MW → 2 MW background.\n\n## What to watch\n\n- Each upward step emits positive JOB SIGNAL events with the configured 30-second lead.\n- The 70 MW level is the workload peak; no 100 MW workload pulse is present.\n- The BESS starts at 100% SoC and provides fast bridge and frequency support.\n- Diesel is configured as 11 × 10 MW, giving 100 MW of required coverage plus one 10 MW N+1 unit.\n- The site is islanded with zero solar and no gas-turbine or utility-import path."
